cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "STMTopRC: MATLAB code for multi-material, multi-volume strut-and-tie topology optimization of reinforced concrete"
abstract: >-
  Ground-structure topology optimization for strut-and-tie models (STM) of
  reinforced concrete. Two one-sided bilinear materials - a tie stiff in
  tension, a strut stiff in compression - share every bar, so the optimizer
  chooses tie or strut from the sign of the stretch. Bar areas are updated with
  a ZPR (Zhang-Paulino-Ramos) scheme supporting per-constraint volume budgets,
  with optional controls on tie location, tie inclination and minimum member
  length. The package is two source files - one that builds the ground
  structure and decides a design, and one that measures, draws and saves -
  plus three study runners. Base MATLAB only, no toolboxes.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-16"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
